/*
 * Declares the SpecialArrayOperatorValue class.
 *
 * SpecialArrayOperatorValue represents a binary operator involving at least one
 * array operand whose evaluation is delegated to a function call rather than
 * performed through the standard operator-evaluation pipeline.
 *
 * These “special” operators include user-defined or intrinsic operations such
 * as `opEquals`, `opCmp`, or any operator that must be resolved through an
 * associated function rather than direct value-level computation.
 *
 * The class encapsulates:
 *   - the operator kind,
 *   - the left and right operands,
 *   - the resolved function call used to perform the operation,
 *   - the resulting static type.
 * 
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::binary::array
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/binary/array.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2023-11-10
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
